{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLr4L5eJ2FYHuWM58RTK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`limit(2**(1/x), x, 0, dir='-')` now returns `0`, and the right-hand limit still returns `oo`. `limit(2**x, x, -oo)` already returned `0` in this checkout, so I didn't change anything for it. `sympy/series/tests/test_limits.py` passes (175 passed, 3 xfailed).\n\nThe cause was in `pow_heuristics` in `sympy/series/limits.py`. It called `limit(...)` without passing `dir`, so the left-hand limit was computed as a right-hand one. I changed it to take `dir` and pass it to each inner `limit` call.\n\nI didn't add a test for the new case."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":769,"cache_read_input_tokens":24215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":769},"output_tokens":220,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b2f5842-3577-4e15-bb6e-cc6ff32ecf7c","uuid":"439bc498-df32-41b8-8ab6-8b5c8c612c07","timestamp":"2026-11-24T00:58:59.604Z","request_id":"req_011ChLr4KPyDjTuRSMnacvLu"}
